@crew tomas
// Head writer 4: career lines. Your bunkmate. He was afraid of staying home; he knows about being afraid.

== career.missed
? tier>=acquaintance
- You were still in your bunk when I left. Are you ill? Should I fetch someone?

== worried.chief
? tier>=colleague
- You saw the Chief? I'd have been terrified. You'll be all right. I can wake you.

== worried.captain
? tier>=friend
- I write to my brother every week. I don't want to write that my bunkmate went.   #serious

== worried.last
? tier>=friend
- I'll wake you. I'm up at six anyway. Please let me, {nick}.   #serious

== career.up
? tier>=acquaintance
- You were up before me today! First time ever. I'm telling my brother.   #funny

== farewell.eve
? tier>=friend
- Your bunk will be empty tomorrow. I'll look up at the star map and think of you.   #serious

== farewell.day
? tier>=acquaintance
- Somewhere new, then. That's brave. You're braver than me.   #warm
- Look out of the window. Wave at the farm moon for me.   #warm

== career.leave.booked
?
- A day off tomorrow? We could do the long way round Deck 2. If you like.

== career.back
?
- Welcome back, bunkmate. I kept your side tidy. Mostly.

// Being ill (head writer 4)
== sick.nudge
? tier>=friend
- You were coughing all night. I don't mind. But please go and see Rina.   #warm
